{:adr-id "2628100000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-4911 (Passenger rail transport, interurban) operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607102200"]
 :mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-4920 (Community Freight Transport, freightops.* Store/Governor/Phase/Operation module shape)"

 :context
 "ISIC 4911 = passenger rail transport, interurban. Live registry.edn :name
  for \"4911\" independently verified fresh: exact, untruncated match
  \"Passenger rail transport, interurban\". NOT a fresh scaffold -- gh api
  confirmed a pre-existing repo cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4911
  already published at :blueprint tier (docs-only: CODE_OF_CONDUCT/
  CONTRIBUTING/GOVERNANCE/LICENSE/README/SECURITY.md + blueprint.edn +
  docs/, no deps.edn/src/test) from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass
  (commit 78c9023, 2026-07-09); this work ADDED the missing implementation
  module set on top of the existing boilerplate, kept not recreated.
  Passenger rail carries a direct-passenger-safety dimension beyond plain
  coordination/logistics -- closed op allowlist must never include an op
  that directly finalizes a passenger-safety-authority decision (signal/
  dispatch-safety interlock override, clearing a train for departure
  after a reported fault); any 'flag a concern' op always escalates,
  never auto-commit-eligible. Also defended from the start against this
  fleet's known bare-noun scope-exclusion self-tripping bug class, acute
  here because :flag-passenger-safety-concern's legitimate purpose is to
  discuss signal/safety/dispatch topics using exactly those words."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a dispatch/signal-safety override (clearing a signal interlock, authorizing departure after a reported fault) -- hard, permanent block, both by forbidden-op identity and by scope-exclusion text scan"
  "direct rolling-stock control or maintenance execution/release -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"
  "flag-passenger-safety-concern never finalizes/overrides/clears anything -- always requires_human_review/advisory_only true, always escalates"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Bare-noun scope-excluded-terms (e.g. 'safety', 'dispatch', 'signal') would
  self-match inside this actor's own legitimate default rationale text
  (:flag-passenger-safety-concern's own default rationale explains 'this
  actor never overrides a signal interlock' using those same words as a
  disclaimer). Fix: scope-excluded terms phrased as the finalization/
  execution ACTION ('finalize the dispatch-safety override', 'clear the
  train for departure', 'override the signal interlock', 'authorize
  departure despite fault', 'bypass the dispatch-safety interlock'), never
  a bare noun -- verified by the dedicated regression test
  mock-advisor-defaults-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion (governor_contract_test.clj),
  which asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for a clean verified
  service, never trip :dispatch-safety-override-blocked and never
  HARD-hold, PLUS a full end-to-end test
  (end-to-end-dispatch-safety-override-attempt-is-held) using a
  deliberately malicious mock Advisor to prove the FULL actor graph (not
  merely the unit-level governor check) catches a compromised advisor
  output on an otherwise-allowed op."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4911 with railops.* (Store/Registry/Governor/
  Phase/Advisor/Operation/Sim), mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4920's
  freightops.* Store/Governor/Phase/Operation shape, adapted to interurban
  passenger-rail OPERATIONS COORDINATION (not dispatch/signal-safety
  authority or rolling-stock control):
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore + DatomicStore (langchain.db),
    contract-tested for parity. Unit of work = service (route + timetable
    slot + consist). :route-schedule-registered? independently set --
    NO op/effect in the closed allowlist can ever set it (only
    with-services/seed-db), so the actor can never self-certify its own
    operating precondition.
  - Registry: pure-function draft-record construction, 4 ops --
    register-service-log (LOG-######), register-schedule-proposal
    (SCH-######), register-safety-concern-flag (SFC-######, always
    requires_human_review/advisory_only true), register-maintenance-coordination
    (MNT-######). Every certificate UNSIGNED.
  - Governor (Rail Safety Governor, matching blueprint.edn's pre-existing
    :itonami.blueprint/governor :rail-safety-governor): 4 HARD checks --
    op-not-allowlisted, dispatch-safety-override-blocked (forbidden-op
    identity OR scope-exclusion text scan, action-phrased terms),
    effect-not-propose (every proposal's :effect must literally be
    :propose), route-schedule-not-verified (applies to ALL FOUR ops).
    ESCALATE: :flag-passenger-safety-concern carries dedicated
    :safety-concern/flag high-stakes stake, always escalates; confidence
    < 0.6 also escalates.
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase 0 read-only; phase 1 = log-service-record +
    flag-passenger-safety-concern, approval-gated -- safety-concern flag
    deliberately writable from the EARLIEST assisted phase; phase 2 adds
    schedule-service-operation/coordinate-maintenance, approval-gated;
    phase 3 auto-commits ONLY log-service-record when clean;
    schedule-service-operation/flag-passenger-safety-concern/
    coordinate-maintenance NEVER auto, at any phase)
  - Advisor (railopsllm): mock-advisor (deterministic, offline); llm-advisor
    seam ready, not wired
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph
    (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval),
    interrupt-before #{:request-approval}, NOT a stub
  - Sim: clojure -M:dev:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow +
    unverified-route-schedule/out-of-allowlist/dispatch-safety-override
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, registry_test, phase_test,
    governor_contract_test (incl. mandatory self-trip regression AND
    end-to-end compromised-advisor regression) -- 33 tests / 157
    assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later
    (pre-existing LICENSE unchanged). README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/
    SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/docs/ all pre-existing, left untouched."

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 4911 interurban-passenger-rail operations-coordination genuinely
    implemented and fully tested, on top of pre-existing blueprint-tier
    boilerplate rather than a wholesale re-scaffold"
   "dispatch/signal-safety-override exclusion hardcoded in governor checks
    (dispatch-safety-override-violations), defended on two axes (forbidden
    op identity AND scope-exclusion text scan), not just README prose"
   "fleet-wide bare-noun self-tripping bug class avoided by construction
    (action-phrased terms) and covered by both a unit-level regression
    test and a full end-to-end malicious-advisor graph test"
   "flag-passenger-safety-concern always-escalate is a two-layer invariant
    (governor high-stakes gate + phase's permanent :auto-set absence),
    writable from the earliest assisted phase"
   "route-schedule-not-verified applies to all four ops and the flag it
    reads can never be set by any op in this actor's own allowlist --
    structurally cannot self-certify its own precondition"
   "portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs; clojure -M:lint 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests
    exercise DatomicStore via langchain.db's in-process API only"
   "mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor protocol
    seam ready for that swap but not wired in this ADR"]}

